# Line endings.
#
# Every blob in this repo is stored with LF, and .prettierrc leaves prettier's
# `endOfLine` at its "lf" default. But core.autocrlf=true is the norm on Windows
# — including GitHub's Windows runners — so `actions/checkout` writes CRLF into
# the working tree and `prettier --check` then rejects every file it looks at.
# That is invisible locally, where the files were authored as LF and never
# re-checked-out, so the check passes here and fails in CI.
#
# Forcing eol=lf makes the working tree match the blobs on every machine, which
# also silences git's persistent "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warnings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must never inspect or convert. The committed native addon is the
# one that matters — a line-ending rewrite would corrupt it — but the image and
# installer types are listed so a future addition cannot trip over this either.
*.node binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
